# Cloudflare Pages rewrites (same-site, 200 = serve without redirect).
# WARNING (Oct 2026, verified live): do NOT add rewrites to .html files
# here. Pages' own clean-URL handling redirects *.html to its clean form,
# so a rewrite to an .html file turns into a redirect:
#  - /restaurant/* -> /restaurant.html became a 308 to /restaurant, which
#    STRIPPED the slug and broke every directory link (storefront showed
#    "restaurant not found"). Storefront links therefore use the query
#    form /restaurant?r=<slug>, which Pages serves directly (200).
#  - /track -> /track.html became a self-loop (308 /track -> /track).
#    /track is now served by Pages' native clean URL (track.html) with
#    NO rule here, exactly like /faq — verify after deploy:
#    curl -I https://ordora.pages.dev/track  (must be 200, not 308)
# Render and Wasmer ignore this file (Express routing).
/app  /app/index.html  200
/app/*  /app/index.html  200
/resources  /resources/index.html  200
/resources/*  /resources/index.html  200
